# Praedixa Distributed Runtime

This repository now supports a two-Mac distributed runtime for heavy downstream forecasting tasks:

- Pro: `MacBook-Pro-de-Steven.local`
- Air: `Macbook-Air-de-Steven.local`
- Scheduler: Dask on the Pro
- Shared study storage: PostgreSQL on the Pro
- Workers: local worker pool on the Pro plus remote worker pool on the Air

The medallion warehouse stays local on the Pro. Distributed execution starts downstream of gold through prepared parquet runtime artifacts synchronized to the Air.

## Quick start on the Pro

```bash
make setup-pro
make sync-air
make setup-air
make start-postgres
make start-cluster
make cluster-status
make smoke-distributed
make prepare-distributed
make hpo-distributed
make backtest-distributed
```

## Remote prerequisites on the Air

Enable macOS Remote Login once:

- `System Settings > General > Sharing > Remote Login`

Then confirm from the Air:

```bash
hostname
scutil --get LocalHostName
ipconfig getifaddr en0 || ipconfig getifaddr en1
```

## Main commands

- `make setup-pro`: local virtualenv + Python dependencies + PostgreSQL 16 check on the Pro
- `make setup-air`: bootstrap the Air through SSH
- `make sync-air`: sync the repo and data to the Air with rsync
- `make start-postgres`: initialize and start the repo-local PostgreSQL 16 instance on the Pro
- `make start-cluster`: start Dask scheduler on the Pro, local workers on the Pro, and remote workers on the Air
- `make cluster-status`: inspect local pids, remote pid, and Dask scheduler state
- `make smoke-distributed`: submit CPU tasks and show which host executed them
- `make prepare-distributed`: build reusable parquet runtime artifacts and sync them to the Air
- `make hpo-distributed`: run Optuna trials through Dask with PostgreSQL shared study storage
- `make backtest-distributed`: run the daily bakery refit backtest in distributed batches, then fit the final model
- `make train-distributed`: run distributed HPO then distributed backtest/final fit
- `make predict-distributed`: score a prepared parquet input in distributed batches

## Dask dashboard

Open:

```text
http://MacBook-Pro-de-Steven.local:8787/status
```

If `.local` resolution is unstable from the browser, use the current Pro IP.

## PostgreSQL notes

- The PostgreSQL instance is repo-local under `artifacts/postgres/data`
- Default port: `54329`
- Default database: `praedixa_optuna`
- Default user: `praedixa_optuna`
- Override the password with `PRAEDIXA_OPTUNA_DB_PASSWORD` before running `make start-postgres` if you do not want the local dev default from `config/distributed.yaml`

## Validation checklist

1. `make cluster-status` shows scheduler plus both Pro and Air workers.
2. `make smoke-distributed` returns tasks executed on both hosts.
3. `make hpo-distributed` writes:
   - `data/optimisation_distributed/best_optuna_params.json`
   - `data/optimisation_distributed/optuna_trials_report.csv`
4. `make backtest-distributed` writes the evaluation artifacts and final model under `data/evaluation_distributed/`.
5. `make predict-distributed` writes distributed batch predictions under `data/predictions_distributed/`.

## Troubleshooting on macOS / Apple Silicon

- SSH timeout or hostname resolution failure:
  - verify `Remote Login` is enabled on the Air
  - try `ssh steven@Macbook-Air-de-Steven.local`
  - fallback to `ssh steven@10.188.88.36`
- PostgreSQL binary missing:
  - run `brew install postgresql@16`
- Dask worker cannot import project code:
  - rerun `make sync-air`
  - rerun `make setup-air`
- XGBoost / LightGBM thread issues:
  - the distributed defaults use `1` Dask thread per worker process and `2` XGBoost threads per task to avoid oversubscription on Apple Silicon
- Browser cannot open dashboard through `.local`:
  - use the Pro local IP and keep port `8787`
